# Example only (nothing installs this). Nightly refresh of the HathiTrust index.
# The time is arbitrary; the job takes whatever update files exist. Times are the server's local time.
#
# `GET /health` shows `"hathitrust_index": false` until the index exists: alert on that.
#
# Install with `crontab -e` as the user that runs the backend, and change /srv/freebookreader to the checkout.
# `flock -n` skips the run if the previous one (a monthly rebuild takes about 4 minutes) is still going.
# The log shows "the index is up to date" on a quiet night; a failure prints "HathiTrust update failed: ...".
30 5 * * * cd /srv/freebookreader/backend && flock -n /tmp/fbr-hathitrust-update.lock venv/bin/python -m app.hathitrust_update >> /var/log/fbr-hathitrust-update.log 2>&1
